{"parentUuid":"8591110d-dc2e-4b15-946a-8a53fe5bc015","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f73187d2-ae51-4903-8e9c-e6c9586ebc16","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nzHv9fsbpYnV6D1RM6Rwe","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"additions\":918,\"baseRefName\":\"feat/entire-review\",\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/285\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFirst of three stacked PRs that rebuild the internals of \\\\`entire review\\\\` (foundation laid in #993). This PR ships the contract-level changes: env-var handshake replacing the marker file, plus the type definitions every later PR builds on. **No user-visible behaviour change** — the legacy \\\\`runReview\\\\` path still drives everything.\\n\\nStack:\\n- **A1 (this PR):** env-var handshake + AgentReviewer/Sink/Event types\\n- A2 → a1: per-agent reviewers, orchestrator, prompt composition, scope detection\\n- A3 → a2: wire \\\\`entire review\\\\` on the new architecture; delete legacy \\\\`review.go\\\\`\\n\\n## What's in this PR\\n\\n**CU1 — Replace pending-marker with env-var handshake** (\\\\`cd4fed9ce\\\\`)\\n- New \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/review/\\\\` subpackage with \\\\`env.go\\\\` defining \\\\`ENTIRE_REVIEW_{SESSION,AGENT,SKILLS,PROMPT,STARTING_SHA}\\\\` constants + \\\\`EncodeSkills\\\\`/\\\\`DecodeSkills\\\\` helpers.\\n- Lifecycle \\\\`UserPromptSubmit\\\\` hook now reads env vars via new \\\\`adoptReviewEnv\\\\`; old marker-adoption path (\\\\`adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto\\\\`, \\\\`sameWorktreePath\\\\`) deleted from the lifecycle.\\n- Pinned JSON wire format for \\\\`Kind\\\\`, \\\\`ReviewSkills\\\\`, \\\\`ReviewPrompt\\\\` on \\\\`CommittedMetadata\\\\` and \\\\`HasReview\\\\` on \\\\`CheckpointSummary\\\\`.\\n- Net diff: **+434 / −472** (deletes more than adds).\\n\\n**CU2 — AgentReviewer interface + Process + Event types** (\\\\`c4b7bced3\\\\`)\\n- New \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go\\\\` defines:\\n  - \\\\`AgentReviewer\\\\` (per-agent contract: \\\\`Name() string\\\\`, \\\\`Start(ctx, RunConfig) (Process, error)\\\\`)\\n  - \\\\`Process\\\\` (\\\\`Events() <-chan Event\\\\`, \\\\`Wait() error\\\\`)\\n  - \\\\`RunConfig\\\\` (Skills, AlwaysPrompt, PerRunPrompt, ScopeBaseRef, StartingSHA)\\n  - \\\\`Event\\\\` sealed sum type: \\\\`Started\\\\`, \\\\`AssistantText\\\\`, \\\\`ToolCall\\\\`, \\\\`Tokens{In,Out}\\\\`, \\\\`Finished{Success}\\\\`, \\\\`RunError{Err}\\\\`\\n- Pure types — no implementations. Implementations land in PR-A2.\\n- Net diff: **+228 / 0**.\\n\\n## Why env-var handshake\\n\\nEach spawned agent inherits its own env, so multiple worktrees and multi-agent runs are correct by construction. Eliminates four bug classes from the prior design:\\n- Worktree race on shared marker file (was [issue from PR #993])\\n- Empty \\\\`ReviewSkills\\\\` on multi-agent runs (HIGH-severity Bugbot finding from PR #1018)\\n- Marker overwrite tripwire (no longer needed)\\n- Refuse-attach-when-checkpoint-missing guard (no longer needed)\\n\\n## Architectural notes\\n\\n- \\\\`review/types/\\\\` lives in a subpackage to break import cycles between per-agent reviewer packages (PR-A2) and the orchestrator (PR-A2). Both depend on this leaf package; neither depends on the other.\\n- \\\\`Event\\\\` is sealed via private \\\\`isEvent()\\\\` method — adding a variant requires editing this file (intentional contract change).\\n- \\\\`Process.Wait\\\\` contract is explicit: \\\\`nil\\\\` on clean exit, \\\\`ctx.Err()\\\\` on cancel, \\\\`*exec.ExitError\\\\` on non-zero, other types for I/O failures. Documented at the interface so consumers can use \\\\`errors.As\\\\`/\\\\`errors.Is\\\\`.\\n- \\\\`Sink\\\\` (will land in A2) commits to **serial-dispatch concurrency** — orchestrator serializes calls even under multi-agent runs (PR-B's RunMulti fans events from N agents into one dispatch loop). Sinks need not internally synchronize.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] \\\\`mise run check\\\\` (fmt + lint + test:ci) green\\n- [x] Per-package unit tests pass: \\\\`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ ./cmd/entire/cli/review/types/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/\\\\`\\n- [x] Integration test \\\\`TestReview_EnvVarAdoptionCondensesReviewMetadataOnNextCommit\\\\` covers the full flow (env set → hook subprocess → state tagged → commit → checkpoint metadata)\\n\\n## Smoke test (env-handshake against real binary)\\n\\nEnd-to-end verification that env-var handshake works on a real binary in a real repo. Procedure:\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash\\ngit checkout feat/entire-review-v2-a1\\ngo build -o /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 ./cmd/entire\\n\\n# Set up a fresh test repo\\nrm -rf /tmp/smoke-a1 && mkdir /tmp/smoke-a1 && cd /tmp/smoke-a1\\ngit init -q && git config user.email a@b.c && git config user.name x\\necho init > README.md && git add . && git commit -q -m init\\n/tmp/entire-smoke-a1 enable --agent claude-code --local\\n\\n# Invoke the lifecycle hook with ENTIRE_REVIEW_* set\\necho '{\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"smoke-a1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"prompt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"}' | \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION=1 \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_AGENT=claude-code \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SKILLS='[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]' \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT=x \\\\\\\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_STARTING_SHA=\\\\\\\"\\\\$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\n  /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit\\n\\n# Verify session state is tagged as a review\\ncat .git/entire-sessions/smoke-a1.json | jq '.kind, .review_skills, .review_prompt'\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n**Expected output:**\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\\\\\\"agent_review\\\\\\\"\\n[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]\\n\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n**Actual output (verified locally on \\\\`feat/entire-review-v2-a1\\\\` @ c4b7bced3):**\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\\\\\\"agent_review\\\\\\\"\\n[\\\\\\\"/test\\\\\\\"]\\n\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n✓ Env handshake works end-to-end on the real