e ENTIRE_REVIEW_* env vars on the spawned\n35\t\t// child process (see cmd/entire/cli/review/env.go) so the agent's\n36\t\t// lifecycle hooks adopt the session as a review session.\n37\t\t//\n38\t\t// Errors from Start indicate failure to construct or launch the process\n39\t\t// (e.g., binary not on PATH at exec.Cmd.Start time, invalid argv). Once\n40\t\t// Start returns nil, errors during the run flow through Process.Events\n41\t\t// (as RunError) and Process.Wait.\n42\t\tStart(ctx context.Context, run RunConfig) (Process, error)\n43\t}\n44\t\n45\t// Process represents a running agent review.\n46\ttype Process interface {\n47\t\t// Events returns a channel that emits structured events as the agent\n48\t\t// produces output. The channel is closed when the process exits — cleanly,\n49\t\t// with error, or via context cancellation. Consumers should range over it.\n50\t\tEvents() <-chan Event\n51\t\n52\t\t// Wait blocks until the process exits and returns:\n53\t\t//   - nil on clean exit (exit code 0)\n54\t\t//   - ctx.Err() on cancellation\n55\t\t//   - *exec.ExitError on non-zero exit\n56\t\t//   - other error types for I/O or pipe failures\n57\t\t//\n58\t\t// Wait must be called exactly once per Process. It is safe to call Wait\n59\t\t// after the Events channel has closed. Consumers must drain Events until\n60\t\t// close before calling Wait; otherwise an implementation that forwards\n61\t\t// parsed events from another goroutine may block while sending.\n62\t\tWait() error\n63\t}\n64\t\n65\t// RunConfig is the immutable per-run configuration passed to AgentReviewer.Start.\n66\t//\n67\t// All fields are optional from a marshalling standpoint (zero value is valid),\n68\t// but Skills is typically non-empty in practice — it carries the skill\n69\t// invocations (e.g., \"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\") the configured agent\n70\t// should run.\n71\ttype RunConfig struct {\n72\t\t// Skills are skill invocation strings passed to the agent verbatim.\n73\t\tSkills []strin