ller notes\n\n**2. Encoding asymmetry — cosmetic.** `EncodeSkills(nil)` returns `\"[]\"` while `DecodeSkills(\"\")` returns `nil`. Round-trip of `nil` becomes `[]string{}` (not nil). Functionally equivalent for `len()` users, but document the asymmetry on the helpers or normalize one direction. Pinning the empty-string-→-nil case in `TestEnvSkillsEmptyRoundtrip` only checks `len`, so the asymmetry isn't pinned by tests either.\n\n**3. `Process.Wait` drain contract is footgun-y.** `reviewer.go:60-62`: \"Consumers must drain Events until close before calling Wait; otherwise an implementation that forwards parsed events from another goroutine may block while sending.\" This is a documentation-only contract — a careless consumer in PR-A2 can deadlock the orchestrator. Consider tightening either the consumer side (\"orchestrator always drains in a loop, then calls Wait\") or the producer side (\"implementations must close Events without blocking on receivers, even on error paths\"). At minimum, every implementation in PR-A2 should ship with a test that proves Wait doesn't deadlock when Events isn't drained.\n\n**4. No compile-time interface check.** `reviewer_test.go:77-79` defers `var _ AgentReviewer = (*X)(nil)` to PR-A2. The interface has a single method, so risk is low — but a renamed method in `AgentReviewer` won't be caught until PR-A2's tests build. If you want a placeholder, a nil-returning `nopReviewer` here would be cheap insurance.\n\n**5. Coverage migration of deleted integration tests is correct.** The deleted `TestReview_MarkerAdoption_WrongAgentDoesNotAdoptMarker` and `TestReview_MarkerAdoption_StaleMarkerIsIgnoredAfterHeadMoves` are replaced by unit tests at `lifecycle_test.go:1050` (`TestAdoptReviewEnv_WrongAgentLeavesUntagged`) and `:1101` (mismatched starting SHA). Equivalent semantic coverage at a lower test layer — a fair trade.\n\n**6. The new end-to-end test is the right shape.** `TestReviewCommand_PassesReviewEnvToSpawnedAgentHook` (review_test.go:106) spawns the real binary with a fake `claude` shim that pipes `user-prompt-submit` JSON to `entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit`. This exercises the spawn → env-inheritance → hook-subprocess chain, which is exactly the integration the env-handshake design depends on. POSIX-only via shell script — windows skip is appropriate.\n\n**7. Defensive env filtering.** `appendReviewSpawnEnv` (review.go:654) strips any pre-existing `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` from the inherited env before re-appending. Good; protects against a parent shell that has stale exported vars. Worth keeping.\n\n**8. State copy + slice-equality compare in lifecycle is correct but subtle.** `lifecycle.go:280-287` copies `*state` into `updated`, mutates, then compares `Kind`/`ReviewPrompt`/`ReviewSkills` to detect changes. Slice headers in the copy are independent of the original (since `adoptReviewEnv` assigns a new slice header), so the comparison works. Fine — but the symmetry depends on `adoptReviewEnv` never *appending* to `state.ReviewSkills` (which would mutate the shared backing array). Today it only does `state.ReviewSkills = skills`, so this is safe; if a future edit changes that, the comparison breaks silently. A `state.ReviewSkills = slices.Clone(skills)` in the helper would lock the invariant in.\n\n### Things that are good\n\n- The `review/` and `review/types/` package split is correct: per-agent reviewers and the orchestrator both depend on `types`, neither on each other. No cycle risk.\n- Sealed `Event` via private `isEvent()` is the right pattern for a closed sum type in Go.\n- The env-var handshake is genuinely better than the marker file — worktree race, multi-agent run skill-list confusion, marker-overwrite tripwire, refuse-attach guard all become non-issues by construction.\n- JSON wire-format pinning tests (`TestCommittedMetadata_ReviewFields`, `TestCheckpointSummary_HasReview`) inspect the raw map after marshal rather than round-tripping — exactly the right shape to catch a coordinated struct+tag rename. Good test discipline."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3494,"cache_read_input_tokens":141880,"output_tokens":2409,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2409,"cache_read_input_tokens":141880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamEXZRvtnGJAkxCm9b84","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5264564-6532-443c-b220-14700567359f","timestamp":"2026-05-06T11:27:23.705Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"d8167230-6b75-41a9-879d-79e6d5be291c","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-v2-a1"}
