{"parentUuid":"59a1fdeb-29ed-4673-b307-f9ce71f55e3d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Lq9EvSHS6LkDib3RLvABqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full stack picture. Below is the cross-stack review focusing on what changes between PRs and what A2/A3 do that A1 alone doesn't.\n\n## Stack-level review: A2 (#1106) and A3 (#1107) in context of A1\n\n### TL;DR\n\nThe stack as a whole is well-thought-out — A2 lands the per-agent reviewers + orchestrator + scope/prompt composition; A3 wires `entire review` and deletes the 1,500-line legacy file. **Two cross-stack issues worth raising before merge**, both about how the stack is *layered*, not the design itself:\n\n### 1. A2 is branched off the wrong A1 commit — silent regression of the agent/SHA checks\n\nA1's tip is `bc53704c0` (\"fix(review): pass review env to spawned agents\"), which added the `EnvAgent != expectedAgent` and `EnvStartingSHA != BaseCommit` verification to `adoptReviewEnv`. **A2's merge-base with A1 is `37f5f0f43`** — the commit *before* that fix. A2's `lifecycle.go` (origin/feat/entire-review-v2-a2:`cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go:981-1000`) reverts to the unguarded version:\n\n```go\n// A2 version of adoptReviewEnv — no agent/SHA checks\nif os.Getenv(review.EnvSession) != \"1\" {\n    return\n}\nskills, err := review.DecodeSkills(os.Getenv(review.EnvSkills))\n// ... tags state.Kind = KindAgentReview unconditionally\n```\n\nThe doc comment even claims *\"No file marker, no worktree race, no scoping guard\"* — actively asserting the scoping guard is unneeded. A3 then re-adds the agent/SHA checks via the same diff that landed in A1's `bc53704c0`.\n\nIf A2 merges before being rebased onto A1's tip, this is a real regression window:\n- A stale `ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION=1` in a parent shell tags any future session as a review of any agent.\n- A SHA-stale env tags the wrong commit.\n- The fix shipped in A1 is silently undone.\n\n**Fix:** rebase A2 onto `feat/entire-review-v2-a1` so it picks up `bc53704c0`. Update A2's `adoptReviewEnv` to keep the parameter and checks; remove the misleading \"No ... scoping guard\" claim from the doc comment.\n\n### 2. Non-launchable agent UX shift — call it out in the A3 description\n\nMy A1 review flagged that the lifecycle hook stops reading the marker file. A3 confirms that this is *intentional, stack-wide*, not a bug to be fixed later: `marker_fallback.go` says explicitly *\"the marker is NOT auto-adopted by anything\"* — the marker now exists only as context for `entire review attach`. So the flow becomes:\n\n| Agent class | Pre-stack | Post-stack |\n|---|---|---|\n| Launchable (claude-code/codex/gemini-cli) | Auto-tag via shared marker file | Auto-tag via env handshake (better) |\n| Non-launchable (cursor/opencode/factoryai-droid/copilot-cli) | **Auto-tag on first turn** | **Manual `entire review attach <id>` required** |\n\nThat's a UX regression for ~half the supported agents. Defensible — the prior auto-adoption had a worktree race — but the A1, A2, and A3 descriptions all say \"no user-visible behaviour change,\" and the parity table at the bottom of A3's description checks every box. Add a row: \"Non-launchable auto-adoption: ✗ (now requires `attach`)\". Otherwise a cursor user upgrading will silently lose review tagging on their first `entire review` and not understand why.\n\n### What A2 and A3 do well\n\n**A2 — ReviewerTemplate is the right factoring.** `template.go` owns Spawn → pipe → parse → forward, leaving each agent file at ~70 lines of just argv + parser. `ProcessError` wraps `*exec.ExitError` with bounded stderr (64KB cap, `[stderr truncated]` marker) — preserves `errors.As`/`errors.Is` while preventing chatty-agent DoS. `ErrTemplateMisconfigured` makes config errors typed instead of nil-deref panics.\n\n**A2 — `classifyStatus` priority order is correctly documented and exercised.** `ctx.Err()` checked before `waitErr` so signal-killed processes during cancellation don't get misclassified as Failed (regression source: PR #1018, called out in the comment). Event-stream signals (`RunError`, `Finished{Success: false}`) override exit-0 process success — catches torn stdout the parser surfaces but the OS doesn't.\n\n**A2 — Codex chrome filter regexes are correctly anchored.** `^exec(?:\\s+\\S.*\\s+in\\s+/\\S*)?$` and `^version\\s+\\d+\\.\\d+...` — narrative containing \"exec succeeded\" or \"version 1.2.3 of go-git\" passes through. Tested.\n\n**A3 — DI via `Deps` is the right cycle break.** `review/cmd.go` only depends on `review/types`, `agent`, `settings`. The two cycle-bound functions (`headHasReviewCheckpoint`, `launchableReviewerFor`) live in tiny bridge files in `cli/`. Adding a new launchable agent is one switch case in `launchableReviewerFor`.\n\n**A3 — Aggressive deletion of legacy detour code.** `--postreview`, `--finalize`, empty review commits, `/entire-review:finish` skill installer all gone. 1,513 + 1,523 deleted lines, single `marker_fallback.go` registry instead of per-agent fallback files.\n\n**A3 — \"1 eligible\" picker shortcut is a real UX fix.** When the alphabetically-first configured agent isn't installed but exactly one other is, use the other one instead of erroring out. Catches the case where a user has hooks for codex but their config still names `claude-code` first from a prior install.\n\n### Smaller things worth a one-line tweak\n\n**A2 — `nolint:wrapcheck` rationale on `Run` construction failure (run.go:50) is wrong but harmless.** The comment says wrapping `err` would break `classifyStatus`'s `ctx.Err()` identity check. But `classifyStatus(ctx, err, ...)` calls `ctx.Err()` directly — wrapping `err` doesn't break anything. Either fix the comment or just drop the wrap-prevention rationale.\n\n**A3 — `runReviewDeps` inner struct (cmd.go:62-64) is redundant.** It carries one field that's already on `Deps`. Inline `deps.PromptForAgentFn` at the call site and delete the struct.\n\n**A3 — `installedNames := make(...); copy(installed)` (cmd.go:210-213) is a defensive copy that buys nothing.** Iterate `installed` directly. (We never mutate it.)\n\n**A3 — `entire review` is still `Hidden: true` (cmd.go:101).** Description says \"user-visible surface preserved.\" With the stack landing the entire rewrite, is the hidden-while-maturing posture still right? Worth deciding before main-merge, not after.\n\n### What I'd do next\n\n1. Rebase A2 onto current A1 tip (picks up `bc53704c0`); restore agent/SHA checks in A2's `adoptReviewEnv`; fix the misleading doc comment.\n2. Add a \"non-launchable auto-adoption removed\" row to A3's parity table and a one-line release note.\n3. Decide whether A3 should flip `Hidden: false`.\n4. Land the stack in order: A1 → A2 (post-rebase) → A3.\n\nOtherwise — merge in confidence; this is a clean three-PR refactor and the design is right."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":194471,"output_tokens":4111,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4111,"cache_read_input_tokens":194471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":864},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamF96SxsFdeA1MeUUEGg","type":"assistant","uuid":"404eb27f-afe6-4ba3-9497-36744897ed32","timestamp":"2026-05-06T11:35:50.999Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"d8167230-6b75-41a9-879d-79e6d5be291c","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-v2-a1"}
